  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{x}{12}+\\frac{1}{3},\\,1\\le x\\le 3\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}x\\cdot (\\frac{x}{12}+\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}+\\frac{x}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{36}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6})|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{37}{18}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
